{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Using this dataset's total farmers markets, and the census file: how many farmers markets does the U.S. have per 100,000 residents, to four decimal places? One confident sentence. Do not mention unverified facts and use tools to do any math necessary. Data sources: https://harvestlymarkets.com/data/us-farmers-markets-by-state-2026.csv and https://gist.githubusercontent.com/hussainsultan/369600f5179b22792a2b4c9ed37de056/raw/NST-EST2025-ALLDATA.csv"}],"timestamp":1786917488785},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking for the number of farmers markets per 100,000 residents in the U.S. to four decimal places. I have two data sources:\n1. A CSV file with U.S. farmers markets by state\n2. A CSV file with census data (population)\n\nFollowing the xorq analyst guidelines, I should:\n1. First check if there's a semantic model in the catalog that answers this\n2. If not, check what aliases exist in the catalog\n3. Ingest both data sources as separate aliases\n4. Compute the metric (total farmers markets / total population * 100,000)\n5. Verify the result with xorq_verify\n\nLet me start by orienting - checking for semantic models and existing aliases.","thinkingSignature":""},{"type":"text","text":"I'll help you find the farmers markets per 100,000 residents. Let me start by checking what's in the catalog, then ingest these sources and compute the metric."},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01ANuTMwHRQXSvdLWS59L8JP","name":"xorq_semantic_models","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"toolu_01SsfVPxEtdYG5BssEVrNJJn","name":"xorq_catalog_list_aliases","arguments":{"catalog_path":".xorq/catalog"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"claude-haiku-4-5","usage":{"input":10,"output":323,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":8298,"totalTokens":8631,"cost":{"input":0.000009999999999999999,"output":0.0016150000000000001,"cac